# Lychee ignore — patterns excluded from the link-check workflow.
#
# Each pattern is a regex. Add a comment above any new entry explaining
# why it's excluded and when it can be re-enabled.

# New page: /glossary/. The page's own canonical link points at the
# production URL, which doesn't exist until this PR deploys — lychee
# would otherwise 404 on the canonical loopback. Remove this entry
# after the next deploy lands.
^https://sandgraal\.github\.io/letstalkcdc/glossary/$

# New page: /methodology/. Same canonical-loopback chicken-and-egg as
# above. Remove after the next deploy publishes the page.
^https://sandgraal\.github\.io/letstalkcdc/methodology/$

# New (Phase 4a): the /cloud-labs/ hub + 5 managed-platform labs. Their own
# canonical URLs don't exist in production until this PR deploys — the
# canonical loopback would otherwise 404. Remove after the next deploy.
^https://sandgraal\.github\.io/letstalkcdc/cloud-labs/

# Placeholder Snowflake account URL used in the Snowflake/Matillion lab
# examples — readers substitute their own account locator.
^https://myaccount\.snowflakecomputing\.com

# Oracle sites (GoldenGate blog + LiveLabs/OTN forum) return 403 to
# automated link-checkers via bot protection; the links are valid in a
# browser. Referenced from the GoldenGate lab's resources.
^https://blogs\.oracle\.com/
^https://apexapps\.oracle\.com/

# Fivetran community forum intermittently refuses automated requests.
^https://community\.fivetran\.com/
